; room-read-band.fk — the phone's permission-free sensors, read and turned into facts.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/room-read.fk
;
; Every input is a reading R5CW20DK17A reported, pulled 2026-07-23 00:32 WITA. No fixtures.
;
; Verdict 1023 when, on Go / Rust / TypeScript / fkwu:
;     1  the integer square root converges (isqrt 101745 = 318)
;     2  total acceleration is 10086 milli-m/s2
;     4  which is 28 per mille ABOVE standard gravity — the sensor's own bias, visible
;     8  and the phone is lying flat within 1374 millidegrees
;    16  linear acceleration, gravity already removed, is 14 milli-m/s2
;    32  which reads as still
;    64  the magnetic field it sits in is 33882 nT
;   128  and the barometer puts it 454 m above the standard sea-level datum
;   256  while the compass claims accuracy 3 (HIGH) and the vector fused FROM it reports
;        heading accuracy -1 (unavailable) — the cell holds both and reconciles neither
;   512  and the live 00:39 posture, propped near 49 degrees, falls outside the small-angle
;        step and is answered -1 rather than the confident 42.9 the arithmetic would give
;
; The teaching is bit 4 and bit 256, and they are the same teaching twice. A sensor at rest
; should read exactly one g; this one reads 2.8% high, and that error is only visible
; because the phone was still enough to have a known truth to compare against. Stillness is
; what makes calibration legible. And bit 256: one organ is confident, the organ built on
; top of it declines to say — both the phone's own words, from one dump, seconds apart.
; Reconciling them would be invention, so the cell carries the disagreement as a value.

(do
    (room-read-check))
